-3145052746","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109197","id":3145052746,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67dbJK","user":{"login":"JanRomero","id":7873027,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4NzMwMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7873027?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JanRomero","html_url":"https://github.com/JanRomero","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JanRomero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JanRomero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JanRomero/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JanRomero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JanRomero/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JanRomero/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JanRomero/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JanRomero/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JanRomero/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-01T16:00:56Z","updated_at":"2025-08-01T16:00:56Z","body":"Good to know, thanks! I’ve thumbed that up. In any case, since it seems the decision was made at some point to not delete files and instead have “Remove” and “Remove Missing”, my issue is pertinent to the “way of doing things” Godot has currently chosen for itself, as opposed to some tractionless proposals for how things might or might not work in the distant future.\n\n(Sorry if I sound defensive, but I guess I am defending the issue ;))\n\nSome more considerations:\n\n* Since you mentioned performance, the actual Godot editor already monitors files for automatic re-import, so it’s neither unheard of nor appears partiularly slow. Idk how many projects people have in their Project Manager, but I’m guessing it’s few enough? I get that the PM should remain snappy, though.\n* I made this an issue instead of a proposal because the button just feels broken when you *know* projects are missing and you can’t use the feature explicitly intended to clean up that exact scenario.\n* To put it another way, the button is essentially one-time use only. Even if you catch it enabled, once you use it it will remain disabled until the PM is restarted. Maybe I’m the only one who finds this weird, idk","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3145052746/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]